# CITATION.cff for the PeakATail TOOL repository (github.com/BMGLab/PeakATail).
#
# Drop-in replacement for the placeholder file currently on `develop`
# (which carries the author entity "PeakATail developers (BMGLab)").
# Validated 2026-09-02 against the Citation File Format 1.2.0 JSON schema
# (citation-file-format/citation-file-format, schema.json): parses as YAML and
# passes jsonschema Draft-07 validation with zero errors.
#
# TWO PLACEHOLDERS REMAIN — both must be filled at release, and BOTH are
# recorded in WD/submission/COMPANION_REPO_PLAN.md:
#
#   1. version: currently "[[PLACEHOLDER: version tag]]".
#      Fill with the git tag cut for the manuscript release (e.g. "v0.3.0").
#      The repo's pyproject.toml declares 0.2.0 and the only tags that exist
#      today are 0.1.a1 / 0.1.a2 — no release tag has been cut yet.
#
#   2. Zenodo DOI: the `doi:` key below is COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE.
#      CFF 1.2.0 constrains `doi` with the pattern
#        ^10\.\d{4,9}(\.\d+)?/[A-Za-z0-9:/_;\-\.\(\)\[\]\\]+$
#      so a literal "[[PLACEHOLDER: Zenodo DOI]]" string in that field makes
#      the file FAIL schema validation. Leaving the key commented keeps the
#      file valid today, and filling it in is a one-line uncomment once the
#      DOI is minted. [[PLACEHOLDER: Zenodo DOI]]
#
# LICENCE: `license: MIT` below mirrors what the repository's default branch
# (`develop`) actually ships today — LICENSE (MIT, added in d146590) and
# pyproject.toml `license = "MIT"`. It is NOT an independent decision. If the
# PI adopts a different licence per WD/submission/LICENSE_DECISION.md, change
# this field to the matching SPDX id in the same commit as the LICENSE file.
# NOTE: github.com/BMGLab/PeakATail `main` still carries GPL-3.0 — see
# LICENSE_DECISION.md §"The conflict you actually have".
#
# A.A.T. ORCID: intentionally absent. The PI stated on 2026-09-02 that it is
# not yet supplied, and CFF forbids anything but a real
# https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX value in that field. Add the `orcid:`
# key to the first author when it is provided; nothing else needs to change.
#
# Author e-mails: only the corresponding author's is included, as printed on
# the manuscript title page. pyproject.toml carries a personal address for
# A.A.T.; it is deliberately not reproduced here — add it only if the author
# asks for it.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PeakATail in your research, please cite both the software (this file) and the paper listed under `preferred-citation`."
type: software
title: "PeakATail"
abstract: >-
  PeakATail (command-line name `ema`) calls poly(A) sites from single-cell
  RNA-seq BAM files using direct poly(A) evidence — reads whose non-templated
  poly(A) soft clips record cleavage and polyadenylation on the individual
  molecule — tiers sites by molecule-counted clip support, filters internal
  priming, and provides an FDR-calibrated, replication-filtered cell-type
  alternative polyadenylation (APA) switch test.
version: "[[PLACEHOLDER: version tag]]"
# doi: [[PLACEHOLDER: Zenodo DOI]]   # uncomment and fill, e.g. 10.5281/zenodo.NNNNNNN
repository-code: "https://github.com/BMGLab/PeakATail"
url: "https://bmglab.github.io/PeakATail/"
license: MIT

authors:
  - family-names: "Amiri Tabat"
    given-names: "Amir"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Computer and Informatics Sciences, Ege University, İzmir, Türkiye"
  - family-names: "Kaymaz"
    given-names: "Yasin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9725-7536"
    email: "yasin.kaymaz@ege.edu.tr"
    affiliation: "Department of Bioengineering, Faculty of Engineering, Ege University, İzmir, Türkiye"

contact:
  - family-names: "Kaymaz"
    given-names: "Yasin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9725-7536"
    email: "yasin.kaymaz@ege.edu.tr"
    affiliation: "Department of Bioengineering, Faculty of Engineering, Ege University, İzmir, Türkiye"

keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - polyadenylation
  - poly(A) site
  - alternative polyadenylation
  - APA

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  status: in-preparation
  title: "PeakATail: precision-first poly(A)-site calling and calibrated alternative polyadenylation analysis in single-cell RNA-seq"
  authors:
    - family-names: "Amiri Tabat"
      given-names: "Amir"
      affiliation: "Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Computer and Informatics Sciences, Ege University, İzmir, Türkiye"
    - family-names: "Kaymaz"
      given-names: "Yasin"
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9725-7536"
      email: "yasin.kaymaz@ege.edu.tr"
      affiliation: "Department of Bioengineering, Faculty of Engineering, Ege University, İzmir, Türkiye"
  notes: >-
    Manuscript in preparation as of 2026-09-02. Replace `status:
    in-preparation` with the published record — adding `journal`, `year`,
    `volume`, `pages` and `doi` — once the paper is accepted. Do not add a
    `year` before publication: a speculative year is worse than no year.
